Spec: Desktop-Gallery

Purpose:
  Provision of a high-performance, cross-platform desktop picture gallery, metadata editor (EXIF/IPTC/XMP), reverse geocoding tool, and cloud uploader for the Crow Web-Gallery ecosystem.

Platform: C++26 (Linux) / C++23 (Windows, macOS), Qt6

Owns:
  ./**

Must:
  Adhere to C++26 standard on Linux and C++23 on Windows/macOS using modern C++ idioms (RAII, smart pointers, value semantics, strong types).
  Follow the layered MVC architecture separating Presentation Layer (Qt6 Widgets/WebEngine), Business Logic Layer (ImageIndexer, Photo/Exiv2 wrapper, regeocode, UploadManager), and Data Persistence Layer (DatabaseManager/SQLite3).
  Execute heavy I/O, recursive folder scanning, thumbnail generation, Exiv2 metadata writes, and network calls asynchronously via QtConcurrent / QThreadPool or QtNetwork without blocking the Qt GUI main thread.
  Maintain synchronized metadata across EXIF, IPTC, and XMP standards via the Photo (Exiv2) wrapper.
  Use prepared SQL statements (QSqlQuery::prepare) for all SQLite operations in DatabaseManager.
  Respect API rate limits via QuotaManager when performing reverse geocoding requests.
  Keep API keys (e.g., re-geocode.ini) and JWT/Refresh tokens out of source code and version control.
  Register all headers containing Q_OBJECT in CMakeLists.txt for Qt AUTOMOC processing.
  Wrap all user-facing UI strings in Qt's tr() macro and maintain translations in i18n/gallery_de.ts and i18n/gallery_en.ts.
  Write all source code documentation, Doxygen comments, and inline comments in English.
  Include a standardized SPDX & Doxygen header (C++ style block comment) with MIT License (SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT) in every source and header file.

Must not:
  Block the Qt GUI event loop with synchronous disk I/O, bulk Exiv2 parsing, or blocking HTTP requests.
  Access the SQLite database directly from UI widgets bypassing DatabaseManager or QSqlTableModel.
  Hardcode external API keys, credentials, or server tokens in source files.
  Manually edit generated files such as include/rz_config.hpp (generated from configure/rz_config.hpp.in via CMake).

